PART 2 — ADDITIONAL DEPLOYMENT CONDITION (NOT PART OF THE MIT LICENSE)
===============================================================================

The following condition applies to any use, deployment, or distribution of
the Software, including modified versions of any module. It is an additional
condition of this license and is not a term of the MIT License in Part 1.

1. Owner account

   Any deployment of the Software must provide an account named "owner" with
   the highest privileges in the system (able to manage terminal accounts,
   perform data maintenance, operate the command console, etc.). Where a
   module implements its own account system, an account named "owner" with
   highest privileges must also exist in that module.

2. Initial password

   The initial password of the "owner" account MUST NOT be a fixed, publicly
   known value. It must be either:

     (a) set by the deployer during installation, or
     (b) generated randomly by the installation process and disclosed only
         once at first startup.

   The owner account must be required to change the password on first login.
   Until the password is changed, access to the management console must be
   blocked.

3. Scope

   This condition requires that the owner account exist. It does not prohibit
   the deployer from creating other accounts, and does not prohibit the owner
   from resetting the password after login.

4. Non-compliance

   A deployment that does not satisfy this Part 2 is not compliant with this
   license.

5. Data protection

   For production environments handling real candidate data, the deployer
   must independently satisfy applicable personal information protection and
   data security regulations. Password leakage is outside the scope of any
   warranty for the Software.

